        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "For the real parameter \\(a\\), the system \\(\\begin{cases}x+2y+z=3\\\\2x+3y+az=5\\\\3x+5y+(2a+1)z=8\\end{cases}\\) has infinitely many solutions when \\(a\\) equals",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The third row becomes the sum of the first two exactly when \\(2a+1=a+1\\), giving \\(a=0\\). The corresponding constants also satisfy \\(8=3+5\\), so the system has infinitely many solutions.",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 21,
