        "quiz_type": "single_choice",
        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "For the real parameter \\(k\\), the system \\(\\begin{cases}(k+1)x+2y=3\\\\2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{cases}\\) has no solution when \\(k\\) equals",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The determinant is \\((k+1)^2-4\\), which vanishes for \\(k=1\\) and \\(k=-3\\). At \\(k=1\\), both equations are identical. At \\(k=-3\\), they reduce to \\(-2x+2y=3\\) and \\(2x-2y=3\\), which are inconsistent.",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 23,
        "question_data": {
          "_meta": {
            "subject": "Mathematics",
